    {
      "label": "Squeeze",
      "title": "The valve opens at the very end",
      "text": [
        "Going down, the piston squeezes the barrel’s air into less and less room. Its pressure only passes the tyre’s, 6 bar, once the air is in a seventh of its first volume: after about 86% of the stroke. Until then the ball valve stays shut and nothing goes in.",
        "So most of each push only squeezes; the last 6 cm or so actually fill the tyre. The fuller the tyre, the later the valve opens."
      ],
